{"version": "2.9.0", "note": "release measurement for 2.9.0 after the community merges. Observation cost: catch-rate 1.0, 0 false positives, VE 9.03 (vs 9.11 last, inside the 3% tolerance). REPLAY TOKENS ROSE 239 -> 278 (+16%) AND THAT IS DELIBERATE, not a regression: #364 adds `unverifiable: {reason}` to an OK replay of a flow that asserts no consequence, and all three passing cost-flows (verify-500 / verify-console / verify-route) are assertion-free, so each now carries the note saying the replay proved nothing. Verified by re-running the identical pass on the pre-merge build (9f961f4c): 220/225/183 there vs 271/276/234 here \u2014 a constant +51 per flow, and verify-modal errors at 323 on BOTH builds (the 'New deploy' button trips the destructive-action guard, which has matched /deploy/ since v2). OPEN QUESTION recorded rather than resolved: the cost-flows being assertion-free means the quoted per-run replay cost is for a flow that cannot fail. The DETECTION passes do carry consequences (grade 'asserted'), so 3/3, 2/2 and 1/1 are sound.", "date": "2026-08-20", "git_sha": "bf30dd10", "layer": "A+C", "measured_cells": 33, "total_cells": 36, "not_measured": ["cross-component-regression/playwright", "cross-component-regression/devtools", "cross-component-regression/reticle"], "per_tool": {"playwright": {"rcr": 0.9, "ve": 6.99, "tp": 9, "real_regressions": 10, "detection_accuracy": 0.909, "false_negative_rate": 0.1, "avg_tokens_o200k": 1288, "p95_latency_ms": 11967}, "devtools": {"rcr": 0.8, "ve": 10.24, "tp": 8, "real_regressions": 10, "detection_accuracy": 0.818, "false_negative_rate": 0.2, "avg_tokens_o200k": 781, "p95_latency_ms": 9899}, "reticle": {"rcr": 1.0, "ve": 9.03, "tp": 10, "real_regressions": 10, "detection_accuracy": 1, "false_negative_rate": 0, "avg_tokens_o200k": 1108, "p95_latency_ms": 13656}, "agentbrowser": {"rcr": 0.0, "ve": null, "tp": 0, "real_regressions": 11, "detection_accuracy": null, "false_negative_rate": null, "avg_tokens_o200k": null, "p